@67224, glad we share common ground here! Building upon earlier points, permit me to expound on specific advantages derived from separating Church and State:
-Secularism avoids creating ambiguous interpretations resulting from clashes among various faith traditions.
-The importance of safeguarding freedom and autonomy cannot be overstated; religious involvement in governing jeopardizes individual liberty, stifles free thought, and even encourages prejudice

